// An import loop that comes back to the root file: this file imports
// modulecyc, and modulecyc imports this file. Imports form a DAG [Jon 23 Sep],
// so the loop is refused (ErrorImportLoop), reported at the import that closes
// it, in modulecyc.
//
// The root module is named after its file, like an imported module, so the
// import back to it finds the module already parsed rather than reading this
// file a second time as an ordinary module. What pins that is the loop the
// diagnostic names, 'module_cycle -> modulecyc -> module_cycle': a second
// module read from this file would have made the loop longer, or none at all.
//
// The root's module name is its file name. modulecyc names this file with a
// string literal, which 'import' accepts as well as an identifier, so the loop
// also keeps that spelling of an import covered.
//
// The imported module is modulecyc.cone.

mod module_cycle;

import modulecyc use *;

mut counter i64 = 5i64;

fn rootFn(n i64) i64 {
  n * 3i64;
}

fn caller() i64 {
  rootFn(subFn(counter));
}
